#pragma once
namespace insim {
inline const char* changelogText() {
    return "What's new in 2.0\n\nHover help: point at any ? to read a short guide without leaving the page. Click ? to pin the guide, and click again or press Esc to close it.\n\nFrame pacing: a new choice under Frame generation. Smooth uses AMD's default timing. Recover after heavy scenes gets your frame rate back sooner after busy airports or thick clouds. Power saver lets the CPU rest. It applies after restart.\n\nFrame rate cap: a new choice under Frame generation. Auto keeps real frames just under half your refresh rate, which is what AMD recommends for smooth frame generation. You can also choose a fixed rate or Off.\n\nMotion source (experimental): a new choice under Image processing. Native uses the motion X-Plane works out for its own reflections, so your aircraft can trail less when you turn or zoom. It works with MSAA, frame generation and the cockpit screen fix. If it cannot run, the normal Camera motion is used and Diagnostics says why. Camera stays the default. It applies after restart.\n\nNo freeze while FSR gets ready: FSR now prepares itself in the background when a flight loads or the window size changes. X-Plane's own picture shows for that moment instead of the sim pausing.\n\nCPU scheduling helper (experimental, Off by default): a new choice under Frame generation. It keeps X-Plane on the faster cores of Intel P-core/E-core processors, or on the extra-cache chiplet of two-chiplet Ryzen X3D processors, and stops Windows from slowing X-Plane to save power. It is undone when X-Plane closes.\n\nDriver pacing: Diagnostics now shows whether AMD's driver can pace frames on your PC, and if not, why.\n\nPerformance per frame: Diagnostics shows how long this mod adds to each frame next to X-Plane's own frame and GPU time. If the frame is much longer than the GPU time, the CPU is the limit.\n\nFor the smoothest frame generation, keep your real frame rate a little below half your refresh rate, use fullscreen or borderless, and turn VSync off with FreeSync on. On Radeon RX 9000 cards with Adrenalin 26.10.1 or newer, AMD's driver can then pace frames for you.\n\nUpdate channels are now called Release Candidates (tested and verified) and Betas (still being tested). Your saved channel is kept. The project is now named xplane12-fsr-framegen on GitHub. Web links to the old name still open. If you came from 0.7.x, its updater could not find this version because of the rename; from 2.0 on the updater handles both names. This version also includes the 0.7.10 performance correction.\n\nFixes from the first live test: history no longer resets on every frame in forward flight, Esc closes a pinned help card, and uninstalling keeps your saved choices.\n\nRetained from 0.7.10:\n\nSmoother scene processing: skip image copies the final scene does not need. This reduces repeated graphics-memory setup. Performance gains vary by scene and computer.\n\nStatus files and live control checks run in the background so slow storage does not hold up rendering. Your saved choices and current FSR, NR and frame-generation options are kept.\n\nThis is a Windows rendering correction. Linux keeps its separate FSR 3.1 preview. Mac rendering is still unavailable.\n\nRetained from 0.7.9:\n\nOptional Discord reports: open Diagnostics, then Preview / send a Discord report. Read the filtered preview, choose a channel and agree before sending. Send now, or once after this session. Cancel before exit to turn the queue Off.\n\nInclude matching X-Plane Log.txt, setup errors, saved image settings and small crash text when available. Original files stay unchanged. Models, DLLs and memory dumps are excluded. Filtering cannot find every private detail, so check the preview.\n\nA Sent status includes a Discord receipt. Uncertain uploads are not repeated automatically. Browser uploads also support Native AA logs. Automatic in-sim submission is Windows-only.\n\nClearer setup and hardware guides, plus a corrected conflict check for empty or disabled known-plugin leftovers. A clean-install warning still needs a fresh log. No new rendering algorithm is added.\n\nRetained from 0.7.8:\n\nRelease includes all current FSR, neural rendering, frame generation and compatibility options. Choose Beta to try upcoming changes. These are the only two update channels. Previous Normal and Experimental selections carry over as Release and Beta.\n\nDownloads now have one clearly named setup executable. Your saved image settings and local models stay in place when updating the same app folder.\n\nRetained from 0.7.7:\n\nSetup now recognizes a verified previous installation of this mod for the same simulator. Updates start with the existing app folder when available. Unknown or edited plugins are still protected.\n\nIf setup fails, it shows the real reason and log location. X-Plane does not have to be running for an ownership error to happen.\n\nRetained from 0.7.6:\n\nLess repeated setup work: the renderer reuses finished image buffers to reduce CPU spikes. This also works when frame generation was enabled at startup and then switched Off.\n\nMore reliable startup: a verified setup link helps the panel find your installation. If needed, Repair startup link fixes the connection. Close and reopen X-Plane after repair.\n\nEasier logs: open Diagnostics > Open log folder. A fresh copy is saved to X-Plane / Output / FSR-Logs after each session.\n\nFirst setup no longer shows a developer's simulator path. Choose your own X-Plane folder. Existing choices are kept.\n\nChoose FSR, independent Native AA or Original simulator as the image processor. Only one mod processes the scene. Restart after switching.\n\nKeep the grouped controls, transitions and help from 0.7.5. The desktop app only updates plugins.\n\nFrame generation pauses while this panel is open. NR and frame generation still cost processing time; this update does not remove every source of stutter.";
}
}
